WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>The Tale of the Three Northern 
Territories Conference</b>

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.980
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.180
With the decree of the previous emperor,

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.780
distribution of lager is 
now permitted freely.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.010
Huh?

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.210
Now, no matter where you are in the empire,

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:46.420
<b>Gernot (37)
 Tax Collector
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:46.420
drinking lager won't be punishable.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:50.800
So that means we can keep serving 
draft beer as we did before, right?

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.790
That is correct.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:54.790
That's great, isn't it Taishou-san?

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.800
<b>Eva (14)
Dishwasher at Nobu.
Resident of Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:55.800
Yeah.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.660
Gernot-san, thank you for 
everything you've done.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.870
If you mean the Backeshof case,

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:04.180
it's not something you need to thank me for.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:08.770
That man was abusing his 
position to enrich himself.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:13.680
I only did what I had to 
do as a tax collector.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.740
That's our Gernot-san!

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:17.020
So cool!

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.300
<i>However, this whatsontap...</i>

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:27.700
<b>Whatsontap</b>

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:27.700
<b>If it tastes good, that's 
all that matters...</b>

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.700
<i>I never could find out 
where it's coming from.</i>

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.640
<i>And the permit to distribute lager...</i>

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.970
<i>It's almost like Izakaya 
Nobu is being protected.</i>

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.910
Is there something you would like to eat?

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:38.980
Today, we'll make anything you want.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:43.490
Anything, you say?

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:44.570
Yes.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.410
Then I'll have the napolitan.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.500
Napolitan?

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.980
What's that?

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.250
You don't know?

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.620
It's the best dish in this place.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.490
I didn't know we had such a dish!

00:01:57.830 --> 00:01:59.440
Um...

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.010
Understood. Napolitan it is.

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:02.010
Gulp!

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:07.510
Shinobu-chan, please tell me later what 
you used my late night snack bacon for.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:10.350
Yes.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:20.180
By the way, our customers were kind 
of excited about some big conference.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.200
Right.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.190
It's the conference between the empire 
and the three northern territories.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:26.520
Three northern territories?

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:27.930
What is that about?

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:32.700
You guys don't even know about that?

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.580
I'm sorry.

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:40.070
<b>Young Mackerel Nanbanzuke</b>

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:40.070
<b>This pickled fish is delicious all the way down to 
the edible bone! The chili pepper gives it a good kick!</b>

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:38.050
Naturally, the territories that are 
beyond the empire's northern border

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.080
are the northern three territories.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:45.010
<b>United Kingdom                            Northern Three Territories                            Grand Duchy</b>

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:45.140
<b>Empire</b>

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:45.140
<b>Eastern Kingdom</b>

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:45.010
The people there have historically 
been unhappy with the empire.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:48.070
For their independence, they 
would go to war if necessary.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:51.080
<b>Count Kaisermark</b>

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:51.080
<b>Count Sistinmark</b>

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:51.080
<b>Count Windelmark</b>

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:51.070
That is the current situation.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.570
This sounds complicated.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:54.310
Yeah.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:57.680
The purpose of the conference was to review 
the cooperation with the empire.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:02.320
Without the discussions going anywhere, 
they went over to the joint meal.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.550
Joint meal?!

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.480
What kind of food did they serve?!

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.600
I thought you wanted to 
know about the conference.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:13.950
It is customary to treat state 
guests with a luxurious feast,

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:17.160
but that day, it was bread, pickled fish,

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.290
and other things you can get anywhere.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:22.110
What was the reason for that?

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.820
It was all according to the wishes 
of the host of the conference,

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:26.700
the previous emperor.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.620
<b>Previous Emperor (78)
Previous Emperor of the Empire</b>

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:32.270
But didn't the delegation get mad 
at being served such a meal?

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:35.460
That didn't happen at all.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:47.620
The entire meal was conducted according to 
the customs of the northern territories.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.570
The delegation was quite delighted.

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:53.430
The people from the northern 
regions eat with their hands?

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:54.140
Yes.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.590
They take flat bread into their 
hand and use it as a plate.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:01.870
It's what they got used to, 
living on the battlefield.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:06.510
Because of that, the three northern 
territories have been mocked by the empire.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:10.220
Since the previous emperor respected 
their culinary culture,

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:13.580
the delegation's stance softened somewhat.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.030
Then the conference was a big success, right?

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.630
Things are not that simple.

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:21.150
The people from the northern 
territories had conditions

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:24.040
for continuing the cooperation 
with the empire.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:27.010
But they were all unacceptable conditions.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:29.470
That is a tough situation.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:35.480
Now, you two, what do you think the 
previous emperor did after that?

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.220
Um...

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.490
He prayed!

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:49.050
Politics is about dealing with things 
that cannot be solved by prayer.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.230
The correct answer is
that he served a meat dish.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:54.180
A meat dish?

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.120
Really?

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:58.370
Yes, a whole roasted calf.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.550
There is an important ceremony in 
 old traditions from up north.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:06.380
Someone of higher standing cuts 
apart the cow and gives it out.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:09.990
It was done to push them to make 
their allegiance to the empire,

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:13.080
or lack thereof, clear.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.620
I-I see.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:19.020
Speaking of, the servers of 
that calf looked like you two.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:21.530
Like us?

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:24.180
Us, serving the calf?

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:30.530
Whole roasted calf is an expensive 
delicacy that you rarely get to eat.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:30.530
Heave ho, heave ho.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:35.510
Everyone at the dinner was 
transfixed by that meat.

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:36.420
However...

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:38.350
This is an important meal.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.340
You must be careful not to drop it.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.280
Yes!

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:44.230
You got it? You must <i>not</i> drop it!

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:45.070
Yes!

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.770
Wh-What have we done?!

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:58.820
Is this our fault?!

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:01.760
Y-You imbeciles!

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.520
Do you even know what you have done?!

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:07.400
You will pay for this crime with your heads!

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:11.830
P-Please, spare our lives! We beg of you!

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:12.840
Please wait!

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.750
With the permission of the previous emperor,

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.800
we have prepared one more calf.

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:22.430
A-Another calf?!

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:26.420
And it's even more impressive 
than the one we had!

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:38.780
The delegation got completely docile 
and retracted all their demands.

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:43.800
Even in the three northern territories, 
a whole roasted calf is not

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:46.570
something you get to have that easily.

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:48.810
They were shown that twice.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:53.120
They must have been awestruck by 
the empire's inexhaustible wealth.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:56.640
So? Don't you think the previous 
emperor's performance was amazing?

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.120
To showcase such power 
without being spiteful?

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.320
Huh?

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:03.560
I feel like...

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:08.240
As long as the previous emperor is 
there, the empire will be stable.

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.830
Here's your napolitan.

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.840
<b>Taishou's Special Napolitan</b>

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.840
<b>With the thick-cut bacon, even 
Gernot-san is fully satisfied!</b>

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:13.080
Oh yes, this is it!

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.710
Taishou, I'd like some Tabasco 
and grated cheese as well!

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:18.250
Gernot-san, you sure know what's good.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:21.740
<i>This is the rendezvous
I have been dreaming about!</i>

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:27.880
So good! But it's even richer than before.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.300
Taishou, what did you do?!

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.400
I added butter at the end.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.900
Butter?!

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:38.890
<i>Pasta, peppers, onion, bacon...</i>

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:42.880
<i>All of that gently enveloped by the 
tomato's umami and the butter's richness!</i>

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:46.400
<i>This is supreme. I would 
even say it's the pinnacle!</i>

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:56.210
<i>And then, beyond the pinnacle, there's agape!</i>

00:07:56.210 --> 00:08:00.130
<i>This is the very reason I was born!</i>

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:04.810
Gernot-san, if you like napolitan so much,

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.140
I'll make it for you anytime.

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:07.530
Really, Taishou?!

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:08.380
Yes.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.340
You're not lying?

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:14.870
I'll have you know lying to a tax 
collector is never a good idea!

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.190
I understand.

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:22.430
W-Well, you already offered, 
and napolitan is quite good.

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:25.460
I suppose I can order it from time to time.

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:29.150
Gernot-san, you have 
sauce around your mouth.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:32.920
I know. I was just about 
to wipe it right now.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:32.150
Here.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:40.420
<i>A-A crest with the three-headed 
dragon and the claws of a hawk!</i>

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:42.260
<i>Th-This is...</i>

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:49.230
<i>Even among royalty, there is only one 
person who is allowed to use this crest.</i>

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:54.410
<i>Only the previous emperor from 
the proud house of the hawk,</i>

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:58.290
<i>who married into the imperial family 
with its three-headed dragon!</i>

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:02.050
<i>I-I get it now.</i>

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:04.910
<i>The mysterious origins of the beer.</i>

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:06.190
<i>The permit for the lager.</i>

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.260
<i>And...</i>

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:11.080
<i>This girl who holds the previous 
emperor's handkerchief!</i>

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:16.180
Eva-dono! I will wash and 
return this handkerchief!

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:17.330
I promise!

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:18.690
S-Sure?

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:22.170
<i>Maybe the napolitan guided me,</i>

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:24.170
<i>but all the dots are connected now.</i>

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.290
<i>This unmistakable elegance.</i>

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:27.690
<i>There's no doubt!</i>

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:31.540
<i>This child is the previous emperor's...</i>

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:38.690
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:38.700
Thank you so much.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:41.110
<i>Taishou-san and the Fräulein.</i>

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:43.970
<i>Those two are absolutely 
the princess' guard.</i>

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:45.470
Gernot-san.

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:47.980
Really, thank you so much.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.360
S-Sure.

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.970
It's quite dark, so please 
be careful on your way home.

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:53.100
<i>Dark?</i>

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.060
<i>I-Is this a warning?!</i>

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:57.340
N-No need to worry.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:59.470
I will never fail to protect 
the princess' secret!

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:02.220
Princess? Who are you talking about?

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:06.710
E-Excuse me.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.220
Maybe he meant me.

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:13.720
<i>All the mysteries have been solved.</i>

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:17.000
<i>Izakaya Nobu is a terrifying place.</i>

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.920
<i>I will carry this secret to my grave.</i>

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.280
Next up, we have Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:39.760
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.110
I love napolitan!

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:40.840
Even if there are leftovers, one 
quick change can transform it!

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:46.770
Ryuuta Kijima is going to put his own 
spin on the dishes featured in Nobu!

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:46.770
<b>Ryuuta Kijima Creates Nobu Dishes</b>

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:55.750
<b>Ryuuta Kijima</b>

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:49.490
Looks like Gernot-san's 
imagination ran wild there.

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:55.750
<b>Grew up in a household where both his grandmother and his mother were culinary researchers,
so he got into cooking at an early age. Now he's a culinary researcher who's popular
for his simple but serious recipes and his fun presentation.</b>

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:52.860
Maybe people with a sharp mind like 
him can actually end up weirdly

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:55.080
overthinking things.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:55.760
I think so!

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:58.350
But it's good that it worked out this way.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:00.500
This is going to be good 
for Nobu going forward.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:02.450
Can't mention Gernot-san 
without mentioning napolitan!

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:04.890
When there's just enough 
napolitan for one person,

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:08.290
splitting it with someone else is a bit sad.

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:14.900
<b>Remix recipe for
small napolitan leftovers</b>

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:11.190
But I think I can make something 
that even Gernot-san

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.860
would probably like by adding 
a certain ingredient.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.870
What do you need to add for 
this wondrous transformation?!

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:19.900
<b>Napolitan Soba-Meshi
 [Ingredients (serves 2)]

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:19.520
Wait, napolitan flavored soba-meshi?

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:22.600
First, this napolitan here...

00:11:19.920 --> 00:13:05.940
<b>Napolitan Soba-Meshi</b>

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:25.920
When it's this long, it can't 
really mix well with the rice.

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:29.410
So use kitchen scissors to cut it like this.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:31.750
If the other ingredients 
get cut, that's fine, too.

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:32.900
Two birds with one stone.

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:38.190
About this length is good, so it 
can mix well with the rice grains.

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:45.190
<b>Making the egg
Mix 2 eggs with a pinch of salt and of pepper</b>

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:41.560
Ah, the eggs make their appearance!

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:45.210
Swiftly whip them up and season 
them with salt and pepper.

00:11:45.210 --> 00:11:49.890
First, we put in the napolitan.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.500
Okay, pasta first.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:52.410
Now the rice.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:53.700
Roger!

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:58.410
Here we need to make sure the noodles 
and the rice are mixed well.

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:01.540
And if you fry this for too long, 
the rice will get sticky and

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:03.710
everything will get mushy,

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:05.850
so finish this up quick.

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:07.680
<b>Once you add the rice, 
don't fry for too long</b>

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:07.110
I see!

00:12:07.690 --> 00:12:11.440
When the rice and noodles are well 
mixed, it should be loose like this.

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:15.510
To finish it up, just like 
Taishou used butter,

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:17.910
I want to copy that and use butter, too.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:19.250
An homage to Taishou?

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:22.310
If you add the butter in 
the beginning, it burns,

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:27.170
but by adding it as a finishing 
step, the butter nicely coats

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:31.230
<b>Add butter at the end and coat 
the rice and pasta with it</b>

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:30.270
the rice and noodles to
make it more delicious.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.230
That smells really good!

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:33.220
Now let's plate it.

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:36.890
The rice and pasta are
such a good match!

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:38.360
So good!

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.400
Now we add the egg to the frying pan.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.330
I've been waiting for this.
I love eggs!

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:49.190
Okay. Only mix it a bit and just 
focus on making a shape.

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:53.650
We take it out while the surface 
is still a little runny.

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:56.650
Jiggly egg! Goes right
 on the soba-meshi!

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:59.720
Add ketchup to taste.

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:01.170
A ton for me, please!

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:04.280
Grated cheese to taste.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:05.120
Bravo!

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:05.950
And it's done.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:09.470
When you only have enough
for one person, with say, napolitan,

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:15.910
<b>Napolitan Soba-Meshi</b>

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:12.600
or yakisoba, and not quite enough to enjoy with multiple people...

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:15.910
If you mix it with rice, everybody can have some.

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:18.950
It's really easy, so please 
do try this at home.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:33.020
<b>Today's high speed footage</b>

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:23.890
Leftover napolitan plus rice and 
butter equals a huge transformation!

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:27.910
Top it with fluffy egg at the 
end and it's irresistible!

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:30.070
I just can't stop myself!

